<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Bautista Sacasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1874–1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Bautista Sacasa was a Nicaraguan Liberal physician and politician who led the Constitutionalist rebellion of 1926–1927 against the Conservatives. Elected president in 1932, he took office as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Marines withdrew, but real power passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anastasio-somoza-garcia">Anastasio Somoza García</a>, commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-dominican-republic">National Guard</a> and his nephew by marriage. Somoza forced him out of office in 1936 and took the presidency himself.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-bautista-sacasa.jpg" alt="Juan Bautista Sacasa" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Underwood &amp;amp; Underwood · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_Bautista_Sacasa_cph.3a44780.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
